  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently underestimates the magnitude of the mid-horizon rally (peaking near 80) and overestimates the depth of the subsequent crash, resulting in a systematic under-prediction of the peak and an over-prediction of the trough.",
    "Implement aggressive mean reversion after spikes: When the price breaks above 75, the model fails to anticipate the rapid reversal; apply a sharp downward correction factor in the 10-15 day horizon following any breakout above 75.",
    "Ignore sentiment signals during trend reversals: Positive sentiment values (0.20-0.33) in the history do not correlate with the model's ability to predict the subsequent rally; treat sentiment as noise during the transition from 68 to 80.",
    "Adjust for lag in volatility capture: The model forecasts a smooth, linear trajectory while the true outcome exhibits high volatility; replace the linear forecast with a range-bound or oscillating pattern that accounts for the 15-day cycle of the rally and crash.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: For the 10-20 day window, reduce the forecast by 5-10 EUR to align with the actual peak timing and magnitude, as the model assumes a steady drift rather than a spike-and-crash dynamic."
